{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact 55139e15d00daf462387ec7cba5a47f2ccc2a892 for request #9796 (git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d29c09faef7e54cdf1199eb86344fa7062d38177). All 23 effective artifacts were individually inspected at this head, with plans/README.md as primary. Revision 3 resolves the remaining P2 in review #9973: an unfounded Room now schedules and executes the bounded local error upgrade, including after remote founding cleanup has already finished.\n\nThe production change routes unfounded work through workUnfounded, and both scheduling and recovery through unfoundedDue. The latter takes the earlier of founding and scrub work. A local scrub failure is isolated so remote founding debt can still settle. Founded scheduling retains the same cursor due time. Migration remains constant-time at open, with at most 500 indexed rows in each table batch, an atomic row/cursor transaction, cursor removal on completion and no later idle writes. Immediate read guards continue to protect projections before at-rest cleanup completes.\n\nArchitecture: the affected Artroom Git publisher/landing and Room storage/alarm code is ordinary Git implementation (gitseq architecture layer 1), coordinated through Workroom application/interpreter and projections (layers 5–7). This preserves the kernel, live nexus and host-binding contracts (layers 2–4). It implements the adopted safe-error requirement without changing protocol meaning, token ownership or signed history. The shared local cleanup step is now reachable in both host states.\n\nSecurity: the closed safe-text grammar and whole-value replacement keep untrusted provider text, arbitrary codes and repository names out of durable and projected errors. Previously retained unsafe rows are drained before and after founding. Existing token IDs, owners, expiries, attempts, retries and signed acts are preserved. Trusted internal table descriptors and indexed paging bound local work; row updates and progress commit together. Independent failure injection confirms rollback and confirms remote founding cleanup survives a local scrub failure. No unresolved security defect was identified at this head.\n\nAuthority: effective planner request #9796 commissions the sink sweep; builder promise #9876 binds the artifacts, and parent mint-B request #9475 has its sealed landing. The original #8651 commission separated contract decisions from implementation requests. Design approval #9463 was ratified and adopted through receipt #9465, and the current merged design artifact #9467 stands. Planner's operator foundation #1 and current roster confirm the request authority, with no retired or dormant source. The implementing/report commits retain the full #9796 Rests-On reference. This is implementation of that adopted decision, without a new delegation or live-operation authorization.\n\nSimplification: one validator, one table-driven bounded scrub and one shared due helper are sufficient. The small unfounded wrapper isolates failure while reusing existing founding settlement. No duplicate cleanup engine or new framework is needed.\n\nValidation: clean disposable clones /tmp/artroom-checker-error-sinks-v3 and ...-guards at the exact head. npm ci, root typecheck and root npm test exit 0: 2,281 passed, one skipped. Separate Git Workers gate: 11 passed. Room bundle dry run and scratch Git harness typecheck exit 0. Logs were read. Fifty-three separate retained/new guard mutations plus two independent transaction/failure-isolation mutations each produced a named runtime assertion failure; compile or load failures were not counted. Some paired Node/Room runs remain green where the companion suite detects the mutation. Sources were restored; subsequent suites pass 19 Node, 68 Room and six independent real-DO controls.\n\nThose six controls cover the original unfounded terminal-row reproduction; 501 rows drained as 500 then 1; cursor-write failure rolling back the batch; 1,001 terminal rows drained through production alarms with a restart between batches; remote founding settlement despite local scrub failure; and a fresh empty unfounded object remaining quiet. Completed cleanup removes its cursor and later work writes nothing. Mutation scripts, results, logs and standalone controls remain under /tmp/artroom-checker-error-sinks-v3*. Scratch tests/configurations were removed from both clones, which are clean. Canonical main is clean at 574568b2c5dfebb1c3b2a30c8afc9b9d7c3719a3.\n\nThis approval binds only this head and artifact set. Mint C revision 3 independently uses migration version 2: the later combined candidate must reconcile migration history and receive exact-head review. Row accounting and the broader product scope remain open. No live deployment, real provider action or credential creation was performed for this review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bdd5ef0e1afd62573e521d0d5ad1e79de14134dc","binding":"assigned","head":"55139e15d00daf462387ec7cba5a47f2ccc2a892","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0e2d0372ec12132cc4cdc69d84560a1c7b765442\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:60d5c3a62d4ea5f8bea1cdb923381a13b10d1d0f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ec1fe5cf4482e4b5ac591a9c96d5372772ab6a5e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}